// Generated by scripts/embed-canvas-guide.mjs from canvas-guide/*.md. Edit those files, then run the script.
/** The Canvas design guide (Canvas's equivalent of Figma's figma-use and figma-generate-design skills), one entry per topic. */
export const CANVAS_GUIDE_TOPICS: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {
 "canvas-use": "# canvas-use: designing in Canvas with the Figma Plugin API\n\nCanvas is a local design tool that runs the **same Plugin API JavaScript you would send to Figma's `use_figma`**. Read this\nonce before your first `runCanvasScript`. It is Canvas's equivalent of Figma's `figma-use` skill, and it only describes what\nCanvas really does. Anything Canvas cannot do yet throws an error in Figma's wording with the way to get the same look; it is\nnever silently drawn wrong.\n\nTopics (read with `readCanvasGuide {topic}`, or the MCP resource `canvas://guide/<topic>`):\n`canvas-use` (this page), `generate-design` (building an ad or a screen from scratch or from a brand), `api-reference`,\n`gotchas`, `text`, `paints-effects-masks`, `vectors-icons`, `components-variables-styles`, `validation-and-recovery`,\n`figma-tools` (Figma's MCP tools and their Canvas equivalents).\n\n## 1. The loop\n\n1. `createDesign {title}` → `{id, revision}` (or `listDesigns` / `readDesign` for an existing one).\n2. `runCanvasScript {designId, expectedRevision, code}` → `{revision, result, logs, warnings, unmeasuredText, created}`.\n   Pass the revision you got last; every successful script returns the next one.\n3. `viewDesign {designId, artboardId, scale}` → the PNG. It is the **same renderer, fonts and crop as `exportDesign`**: at one\n   scale it is byte-for-byte the export, so what you check is what ships.\n4. `getDesignMetadata {designId, nodeId?, depth?}` → an XML outline (ids, types, names, geometry, rotation, fills, text, font,\n   masks, effects), like Figma's `get_metadata`. Use it to check structure without a screenshot.\n5. Fix with another script (find nodes by id or name) and check again. Then `exportDesign {designId, artboardId, scale}`.\n\n## 2. Critical rules\n\n1. **The code is the body of an async function.** Use top-level `await` and `return`. Do not wrap it in an IIFE and do not call\n   `figma.closePlugin()` (it is accepted and does nothing).\n2. **`return` is your output channel.** Return every created or changed node id (`return { frame: frame.id, created: [...] }`).\n   Unlike Figma, `console.log` output does come back (in `logs`), but `return` is what later calls should rely on.\n3. **A script is all or nothing.** If it throws, nothing is saved and the revision does not change, so it is always safe to fix\n   the error and run it again. Errors carry the script's line number.\n4. **Colours are 0–1**: `{ r: 1, g: 0.4, b: 0 }`. Put transparency on the paint (`{ type: 'SOLID', color, opacity: 0.5 }`).\n   `figma.util.rgb('#ff6600')` and `figma.util.solidPaint('#ff6600', { opacity: 0.5 })` convert hex.\n5. **Fills, strokes and effects are arrays you replace**: copy, change, reassign (`node.fills = [...]`). Changing an item of\n   the array you read has no effect, as in Figma.\n6. **Load every font before you touch text**: `await figma.loadFontAsync({ family: 'Poppins', style: 'SemiBold' })`. Any Google\n   font installs itself on first use, with all its weights and italics; Inter is built in. Brand fonts that are not on Google\n   are uploaded once per project with `uploadDesignFont {source: '/path/Brand-Bold.otf'}` and then load the same way.\n   Style names are Figma's: `Thin`, `ExtraLight`, `Light`, `Regular`, `Medium`, `SemiBold`, `Bold`, `ExtraBold`, `Black`, plus\n   `Italic` (`Bold Italic`). A style the family lacks throws `Font \"X Y\" has no such style. Installed styles: …`.\n   There is no limit on how many fonts a project uses.\n7. **`resize()` sets both sizing modes to FIXED**, exactly as Figma does. Call `resize()` first, then set\n   `primaryAxisSizingMode` / `counterAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'` or `layoutSizing* = 'HUG'`. A frame resized after you asked it to\n   hug stays at the size you passed.\n8. **`layoutSizingHorizontal/Vertical = 'FILL'` needs an auto-layout parent**: `appendChild` first, then set FILL. `HUG` is for\n   auto-layout frames and for text. `primaryAxisSizingMode`/`counterAxisSizingMode` take `FIXED | AUTO`; `layoutSizing*` take\n   `FIXED | HUG | FILL`. Do not mix the two enums.\n9. **Wrapping text** needs `textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT'` and a width (`resize(width, h)` or FILL in an auto-layout parent).\n   The default `WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT` never wraps.\n10. **Use auto layout for anything whose children relate** (stacks, rows, chips, cards, buttons): `figma.createAutoLayout('VERTICAL', { itemSpacing: 12 })`.\n    Use absolute `x`/`y` for free composition on an ad (a sticker on a photo), or `layoutPositioning = 'ABSOLUTE'` inside an\n    auto-layout frame.\n11. **Put top-level frames side by side**, not all at (0, 0): read `figma.currentPage.children` and place the new frame to the\n    right of the last one (`x = last.x + last.width + 120`).\n12. **Pictures come from files, URLs or data URLs**: `const img = await figma.createImageAsync('/abs/photo.jpg')`, then\n    `{ type: 'IMAGE', imageHash: img.hash, scaleMode: 'FILL' }`. `figma.createImage(bytes)` is not available.\n13. **`await` every promise** (`loadFontAsync`, `createImageAsync`, `getNodeByIdAsync`, `getLocal…Async`).\n14. **One page.** A Canvas design has one page here; `figma.createPage()` adds to the current page with a warning.\n15. **Read the warnings and `unmeasuredText`** in every result. A warning means something was approximated (it says what to do\n    instead); `unmeasuredText` lists text that could not be measured (a missing font or glyph).\n\n## 3. Efficient APIs (same as `use_figma`)\n\n- `figma.createAutoLayout(direction?, props?)`: an auto-layout frame hugging both axes. `figma.createAutoLayout('VERTICAL', { name: 'Card', itemSpacing: 12, paddingTop: 24 })`.\n- `node.set(props)`: many properties in one call; `layoutMode` is applied first, `width`/`height` go through `resize()`.\n- `node.query(selector)` / `figma.currentPage.query(selector)`: CSS-like search inside the subtree.\n  Types (`TEXT`, `FRAME`, `INSTANCE`…), `#id`, `[name=Card]`, `[name^=Head]`, `[name*=art]`, `[name$=Nav]`, dot paths with `*`\n  (`[fills.0.type=SOLID]`, `[mainComponent.name=Button]`), combinators (`A B`, `A > B`, `A + B`, `A ~ B`), `,`, `*`,\n  `:first-child`, `:last-child`, `:nth-child(n)`, `:not(…)`, `:is(…)`, `:where(…)`. The result has `length`, `first()`,\n  `last()`, `toArray()`, `each()`, `map()`, `filter()`, `values(['name','x'])`, `set(props)`, `query()` and is iterable.\n- `node.placeholder = true/false` is accepted (Canvas has nothing to shimmer; it is never drawn or exported).\n- `node.screenshot()` cannot return a picture from a Canvas script: call `viewDesign` after the script.\n\nCanvas extras:\n- `canvas.icon(name, { color, size, strokeWidth })` returns SVG markup for `figma.createNodeFromSvg`: 67 line icons (search,\n  star, check, x, arrows, chevrons, heart, thumbs-up, phone, mail, map-pin, clock, users, cart, shield-check, bar-chart, …) and\n  brand marks (`google-g` in four colours, google, google-maps, facebook, instagram, tiktok, youtube, x, apple, shopify,\n  whatsapp, pinterest, reddit, spotify, trustpilot, stripe, paypal). `canvas.icons('arrow')` or `listDesignIcons {query}` lists names.\n\n## 4. Incremental workflow\n\n- Build a whole ad in one script when you can; it is atomic, so a failure costs nothing. Split only when a script would be\n  very long or when you want to look before continuing.\n- Return ids and the facts you need next (sizes, counts). No state survives between scripts: pass ids as string literals.\n- Order inside a script: fonts → pictures → the top frame (resize, fills, clip) → sections as auto-layout frames → text →\n  free-floating decorations (stickers, arrows, badges) → effects.\n- After composing, take one `viewDesign` at `scale: 0.5` (9:16 ads) or `1` (1:1), look properly (clipped words, overlaps,\n  wrong wraps, missing pictures), fix, and look once more. Stop when it passes.\n\n## 5. Pre-flight checklist\n\n- [ ] Every font loaded with `await` before text is created or changed; style names spelled as Figma spells them.\n- [ ] Colours 0–1, opacity on the paint.\n- [ ] `resize()` before AUTO/HUG; FILL only after `appendChild` into an auto-layout frame.\n- [ ] Wrapping text: `textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT'` plus a width.\n- [ ] Pictures through `figma.createImageAsync`.\n- [ ] New top-level frame placed away from existing ones; returns all ids.\n- [ ] After the run: no warnings you did not expect, `unmeasuredText` empty.\n\n## 6. Error recovery\n\n- The script threw: nothing changed. Read the message (it names the property and the fix), correct it, run again with the\n  same `expectedRevision`.\n- `expectedRevision` mismatch: someone (or a previous call) changed the design. `readDesign` or `getDesignMetadata` for the\n  current revision and state, then continue.\n- It ran but looks wrong: `getDesignMetadata {nodeId}` for geometry, then a small script that changes only that node.\n- `TypeError: object is not extensible: … has no property \"x\"`: a misspelt or non-Figma property name.\n- `x is not supported in Canvas yet. …`: a real Figma feature Canvas lacks; the message says what to use instead.\n\n## 7. Discover before you create\n\n- `getDesignSystem {designId}`: components, text styles, variables (per mode) and named layers per frame.\n- `getStyleGuide`: the project's brand colours, fonts and voice.\n- `listDesignTemplates {query}` / `insertDesignTemplate`: ready ad layouts (product hero, benefit callouts, testimonial, us vs\n  them, before/after, offer, founder quote, UGC post) in 1:1, 4:5 and 9:16.\n- In a script: `figma.currentPage.query('FRAME').values(['name','width','height'])`, `await figma.getLocalTextStylesAsync()`,\n  `(await figma.variables.getLocalVariableCollectionsAsync())[0]`.\n\n## 8. Snippets\n\nAd frame with a photo, a dark gradient wash and a headline:\n\n```js\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({ family: 'DM Sans', style: 'Bold' })\nconst photo = await figma.createImageAsync('/abs/street.jpg')\nconst ad = figma.createFrame()\nad.name = 'Ad 9:16'; ad.resize(1080, 1920); ad.clipsContent = true\nad.fills = [{ type: 'IMAGE', imageHash: photo.hash, scaleMode: 'FILL' }]\nconst wash = figma.createRectangle(); ad.appendChild(wash); wash.resize(1080, 1920)\nwash.fills = [{ type: 'GRADIENT_LINEAR', gradientTransform: [[0, 1, 0], [-1, 0, 1]],\n  gradientStops: [{ position: 0, color: { r: 0.03, g: 0.06, b: 0.16, a: 0.9 } }, { position: 0.6, color: { r: 0.03, g: 0.06, b: 0.16, a: 0 } }] }]\nconst head = figma.createText(); ad.appendChild(head)\nhead.fontName = { family: 'DM Sans', style: 'Bold' }; head.fontSize = 88\nhead.lineHeight = { unit: 'PERCENT', value: 105 }; head.letterSpacing = { unit: 'PERCENT', value: -2 }\nhead.characters = 'Get found on Google'\nhead.textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT'; head.resize(920, 100); head.x = 80; head.y = 260\nhead.fills = [figma.util.solidPaint('#ffffff')]\nreturn { frame: ad.id }\n```\n\nA rotated sticker with a shadow, sized by its text:\n\n```js\nconst tag = figma.createAutoLayout('HORIZONTAL', { name: 'Sticker', paddingLeft: 28, paddingRight: 28, paddingTop: 14, paddingBottom: 14, cornerRadius: 14 })\nad.appendChild(tag)\ntag.fills = [figma.util.solidPaint('#ffd400')]\ntag.effects = [{ type: 'DROP_SHADOW', color: { r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 0.3 }, offset: { x: 0, y: 8 }, radius: 24, spread: 0, visible: true, blendMode: 'NORMAL' }]\nconst label = figma.createText(); tag.appendChild(label)\nlabel.fontName = { family: 'DM Sans', style: 'Bold' }; label.fontSize = 44; label.characters = '47% OFF'\ntag.rotation = -8; tag.x = 640; tag.y = 1180\n```\n\nOne text with a coloured word and a second font:\n\n```js\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({ family: 'Inter', style: 'Regular' })\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({ family: 'Noto Serif', style: 'Italic' })\nconst t = figma.createText(); t.fontName = { family: 'Inter', style: 'Regular' }; t.fontSize = 64\nt.characters = 'Show up on Google & ChatGPT'\nconst at = t.characters.indexOf('Google')\nt.setRangeFills(at, at + 6, [figma.util.solidPaint('#1a73e8')])\nt.setRangeFontName(at, at + 6, { family: 'Noto Serif', style: 'Italic' })\n```\n",
 "generate-design": "# generate-design: building an ad (or a screen) in Canvas\n\nThe Canvas counterpart of Figma's `figma-generate-design`. Use it when you design from a brief, rebuild a reference ad, or\nlay out a new frame from a brand. Read `canvas-use` first.\n\n## Step 1: understand the deliverable\n- Size: 1:1 1080×1080 (feed), 4:5 1080×1350 (feed), 9:16 1080×1920 (Stories/Reels; keep words out of the top 270 px and\n  bottom 670 px), or the reference's exact size.\n- The one message the ad must land, the proof it shows (stars, numbers, UI, before/after) and the action.\n- If there is a reference image, list its parts top to bottom: background (photo, colour, gradient), headline, sub-lines, UI\n  mock-ups, stickers/badges, arrows/handwriting, logo. Note fonts (match them to a Google family), colours (hex), sizes as a\n  share of the frame, rotations, shadows and blurs.\n\n## Step 2: collect what the project already has\n- `getStyleGuide`: brand colours, fonts, voice.\n- `getDesignSystem {designId}`: components, text styles, variables and their modes, named layers per frame.\n- `listDesignTemplates {query}`: a ready layout may cover most of the ad; insert it and re-brand rather than draw it again.\n- Pictures: use the project's own photos and product shots (`createImageAsync` with their paths). Brand marks and icons come\n  from `canvas.icon(...)`; never redraw a logo from primitives.\n- Fonts: load every family you need at the top of the script. Upload brand fonts once (`uploadDesignFont`).\n\n## Step 3: the frame\n```js\nfor (const n of figma.currentPage.children.filter(n => n.name === 'Ad / Google 9:16')) n.remove()   // idempotent re-runs\nconst last = figma.currentPage.children.at(-1)\nconst ad = figma.createFrame(); ad.name = 'Ad / Google 9:16'; ad.resize(1080, 1920); ad.clipsContent = true\nad.x = last ? last.x + last.width + 120 : 0; ad.y = 0\n```\nBackground first (picture fill with `scaleMode: 'FILL'`, or a gradient), then washes and tone layers (gradients, MULTIPLY /\nSOFT_LIGHT rectangles), then content.\n\n## Step 4: the content, section by section\n- Group related pieces into auto-layout frames (`figma.createAutoLayout`) so text changes reflow: a headline block, a search\n  bar (icon + query), a result card (title, stars row, meta), a chip list, a CTA button. Place each block with `x`/`y` on\n  the ad, or stack them in one vertical auto-layout column with `SPACE_BETWEEN`.\n- Repeated pieces (chips, notification cards, list rows, stat cards) are a component plus instances; override only the text\n  and visibility of instance layers.\n- UI mock-ups on a phone or laptop screen: a frame sized to the screen area, `clipsContent`, `cornerRadius` (and\n  `cornerSmoothing: 0.6` for iOS), placed over the photo's screen; draw the UI inside at real proportions.\n- Free decorations last: rotated stickers (auto-layout pill, rotation, drop shadow), handwritten notes (Caveat or another\n  script font, rotated), hand-drawn arrows (`createNodeFromSvg` with a round-capped path), circular zooms (an ellipse mask or\n  a round clipping frame with a thick ring).\n- Effects: drop shadows for lift (radius 16–40, alpha 0.15–0.35), `BACKGROUND_BLUR` for frosted panels, `LAYER_BLUR` for glows.\n- Colour in one word: `setRangeFills` on the same text; a second font in one line: `setRangeFontName`.\n- Emoji go straight into `characters` (they draw in colour).\n\n## Step 5: validate\n1. Read `warnings` and `unmeasuredText` from the script result: fix anything listed.\n2. `viewDesign {artboardId, scale: 0.5}` (9:16) or `scale: 1` (1:1). Compare with the reference side by side in your head:\n   layout and proportions, type sizes and weights, colours, what is in front of what.\n3. One fix script for everything you saw, then one more look. Stop when it matches.\n4. `exportDesign {artboardId, scale: 1}`.\n\n## Step 6: updating an existing ad\n`getDesignMetadata {designId, nodeId: adId}` for its structure, then a script that finds the layers by name\n(`ad.query('TEXT[name=Headline]').first()`) and changes only them. Keep ids stable; do not rebuild unless the layout changes.\n\n## Best practices\n- Reach for whatever Plugin API feature expresses the design best; Canvas supports the same set for ads, and refuses (with an\n  alternative) rather than drawing something wrong.\n- One script per ad is normal; it is atomic and fast (1–5 s).\n- Name layers for what they are (`Headline`, `Search bar`, `Sticker`), so later edits and templates can find them.\n- Keep component masters off the artboard (below it), so exports stay clean.\n- $0 rule: reuse the project's pictures; do not generate images unless the user asked and approved.\n",
 "api-reference": "# api-reference: what `runCanvasScript` supports\n\nNames, units and behaviour follow the Figma Plugin API. \"Throws\" means the call fails with Figma-style wording and the way to\nget the same look; nothing is ever accepted and then silently dropped.\n\n## figma global\n\n| Area | Supported |\n|---|---|\n| Create | `createFrame`, `createAutoLayout(direction?, props?)`, `createRectangle`, `createEllipse`, `createText`, `createLine`, `createStar`, `createPolygon`, `createVector`, `createComponent`, `createComponentFromNode(frameOrGroup)`, `createNodeFromSvg(svg)`, `createTextStyle`, `createImageAsync(path \\| https URL \\| data URL)` |\n| Combine | `group(nodes, parent, index?)`, `union` / `subtract` / `intersect` / `exclude(nodes, parent, index?)` (real boolean shapes) |\n| Find | `currentPage.children`, `currentPage.findOne/findAll/findChild/findChildren/findAllWithCriteria({types})`, `currentPage.query(selector)`, `getNodeById`, `getNodeByIdAsync`, `root.findAll` |\n| Fonts | `loadFontAsync({family, style})` (installs any Google font), `listAvailableFontsAsync()` (the loaded faces) |\n| Pictures | `createImageAsync(source)` → `{hash, getSizeAsync()}`, `getImageByHash(hash)` |\n| Styles | `getLocalTextStyles(Async)`, `getStyleById(Async)`, `createTextStyle`; `getLocalPaintStyles` / `getLocalEffectStyles` return `[]` |\n| Variables | `figma.variables.getLocalVariableCollections(Async)`, `getVariableCollectionById`, `getLocalVariables(Async)(type?)`, `getVariableById(Async)`, `createVariableCollection`, `createVariable(name, collection, 'COLOR' \\| 'FLOAT')`, `setBoundVariableForPaint(paint, 'color', v)` (returns a new paint), `setBoundVariableForEffect` |\n| Util | `figma.util.rgb('#hex')`, `rgba('#hex' or '#hexaa')`, `solidPaint('#hex', overrides?)`, `figma.mixed` |\n| Other | `notify` (logged), `viewport` (inert), `commitUndo`, `closePlugin` (no-ops), `createPage` (adds to the current page, warns) |\n| Canvas | `canvas.icon(name, {color, size, strokeWidth})` → SVG for `createNodeFromSvg`; `canvas.icons(query)` → names |\n\nThrows with a hint: `combineAsVariants`, `createComponentSet` (one component per variant + `swapComponent`),\n`importComponentByKeyAsync` / `importComponentSetByKeyAsync` / `importStyleByKeyAsync` (no team libraries: use\n`getDesignSystem`, templates), `createPaintStyle` (bind a COLOR variable), `createEffectStyle` (set `effects`),\n`createGridStyle`, `createSection`, `createSlice`, `createTextPath`, `createImage(bytes)` (use `createImageAsync`),\n`flatten` (use `union`), `exportAsync` (use `viewDesign` / `exportDesign`).\n\n## Every node\n\n`id`, `type`, `name`, `parent`, `children`, `visible`, `locked`, `removed`, `remove()`, `clone()`, `set(props)`, `query(selector)`,\n`findOne/findAll/findChild/findChildren/findAllWithCriteria/findOneWithCriteria`, `getPluginData/setPluginData`,\n`getSharedPluginData/setSharedPluginData`, `toJSON()`.\n\nGeometry: `x`, `y`, `width`, `height` (read: measured), `resize(w, h)` and `resizeWithoutConstraints` (both set Fixed sizing),\n`rotation` (degrees, counter-clockwise, around the top-left corner as in Figma), `relativeTransform` (rotation and flips;\nskew or scale throws and points to `resize`), `absoluteTransform`, `absoluteBoundingBox`, `absoluteRenderBounds`,\n`constraints {horizontal, vertical: MIN | MAX | CENTER | STRETCH | SCALE}`, `lockAspectRatio()` / `unlockAspectRatio()`,\n`targetAspectRatio`.\n\nAppearance: `opacity`, `blendMode` (all 16 Figma modes, plus `PASS_THROUGH`), `fills`, `strokes`, `strokeWeight`,\nper-side `strokeTopWeight/Right/Bottom/Left`, `strokeAlign INSIDE | CENTER | OUTSIDE`, `strokeCap`, `strokeJoin MITER | ROUND | BEVEL`,\n`strokeMiterLimit`, `dashPattern`, `cornerRadius` and `topLeftRadius/topRightRadius/bottomLeftRadius/bottomRightRadius`,\n`cornerSmoothing` (0–1, iOS squircle), `clipsContent`, `effects`, `isMask`, `maskType ALPHA | VECTOR | LUMINANCE`,\n`setBoundVariable(field, variable)` for `cornerRadius`, `itemSpacing`, paddings, `strokeWeight`, `fontSize`, `lineHeight`,\n`letterSpacing`, `paragraphSpacing`, radii; `boundVariables`; `setExplicitVariableModeForCollection(collection, modeId)`,\n`clearExplicitVariableModeForCollection`, `explicitVariableModes`.\n\nAccepted and ignored because they never show in an exported ad: `expanded`, `exportSettings`, `reactions`,\n`constrainProportions`, `description`, `documentationLinks`, `guides`, `relaunchData`, `annotations`, `devStatus`,\n`placeholder`. Everything else that is not listed here throws (`object is not extensible: … has no property \"x\"`), so a typo\nnever passes silently.\n\n## Frames, components and auto layout\n\n`layoutMode NONE | HORIZONTAL | VERTICAL`, `itemSpacing`, `counterAxisSpacing`, `paddingTop/Right/Bottom/Left`,\n`horizontalPadding`, `verticalPadding`, `primaryAxisAlignItems MIN | CENTER | MAX | SPACE_BETWEEN`,\n`counterAxisAlignItems MIN | CENTER | MAX | BASELINE`, `counterAxisAlignContent AUTO | SPACE_BETWEEN`,\n`primaryAxisSizingMode` / `counterAxisSizingMode FIXED | AUTO`, `layoutWrap NO_WRAP | WRAP`, `itemReverseZIndex`,\n`minWidth`, `maxWidth`, `minHeight`, `maxHeight`; children: `layoutSizingHorizontal` / `layoutSizingVertical FIXED | HUG | FILL`,\n`layoutGrow`, `layoutAlign INHERIT | STRETCH`, `layoutPositioning AUTO | ABSOLUTE`.\n`appendChild(node)`, `insertChild(index, node)`.\n\nComponents: `createComponent()`, `component.createInstance()`, `instance.mainComponent`, `getMainComponentAsync()`,\n`instance.detachInstance()`, `instance.swapComponent(component)`. An instance's layers are reachable (`instance.children`,\n`instance.findOne(...)`, ids `I<instance>;<layer>`): setting `characters`, `visible`, text range styles or a nested swap on them\nstores an override; anything else on an instance layer throws and says to `detachInstance()` first.\nNot yet: variants, component properties (`setProperties`, `addComponentProperty` throw with the alternative).\n\n## Text\n\n`characters`, `fontName`, `fontSize`, `fontWeight` (read), `lineHeight {unit: PIXELS | PERCENT | AUTO, value}`,\n`letterSpacing {unit: PIXELS | PERCENT, value}`, `paragraphSpacing`, `textAlignHorizontal LEFT | CENTER | RIGHT | JUSTIFIED`,\n`textAlignVertical TOP | CENTER | BOTTOM`, `textAutoResize WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT | HEIGHT | NONE | TRUNCATE`,\n`textTruncation DISABLED | ENDING`, `maxLines`, `textCase ORIGINAL | UPPER | LOWER`, `textDecoration NONE | UNDERLINE | STRIKETHROUGH`,\n`textStyleId`. Ranges: `setRangeFills`, `setRangeFontName`, `setRangeFontSize`, `setRangeTextDecoration`, `setRangeLetterSpacing`,\n`setRangeLineHeight`, `getStyledTextSegments(fields)`. Colour emoji and symbols draw from fallback fonts.\nThrows with a hint: `paragraphIndent`, `listSpacing`, `hangingPunctuation`, `hangingList`, `leadingTrim`, `textCase TITLE / SMALL_CAPS`.\n\n## Paints and effects\n\nPaints: `SOLID`, `GRADIENT_LINEAR`, `GRADIENT_RADIAL` (with `gradientTransform` and `gradientStops`), `IMAGE`\n(`scaleMode FILL | FIT | CROP | TILE | STRETCH`, `imageTransform` for CROP, `scalingFactor` for TILE, `rotation`, `filters\n{exposure, contrast, saturation, temperature, tint, highlights, shadows}` each −1..1), each with `opacity`, `visible`, `blendMode`.\n`GRADIENT_ANGULAR`, `GRADIENT_DIAMOND`, `VIDEO` and `PATTERN` throw.\nEffects: `DROP_SHADOW`, `INNER_SHADOW` (`color`, `offset`, `radius`, `spread`, `visible`), `LAYER_BLUR`, `BACKGROUND_BLUR`\n(`radius`, `blurType NORMAL`). Progressive blur, `NOISE`, `TEXTURE` and `GLASS` throw.\n\n## Vectors\n\n`createVector()` + `vectorPaths = [{ windingRule: 'NONZERO' | 'EVENODD', data: 'M0 0 L10 10 C… Z' }]` (any SVG path syntax),\n`createStar` (`pointCount`, `innerRadius`), `createPolygon` (`pointCount`), `createLine` (a 1 px line along x; `strokeWeight`,\n`strokes`, `rotation`), `createNodeFromSvg` (paths, basic shapes, `<g>` transforms, viewBox, `<use>`, strokes with caps/joins/\ndashes, opacity, linear and radial gradient fills; text, images, filters, clip paths and masks inside the SVG are reported in\n`warnings`). `vectorNetwork`, `arcData` and `outlineStroke()` throw with the SVG alternative.\n\n## Operations around the script\n\n`createDesign`, `listDesigns`, `readDesign`, `getDesignSystem`, `getDesignMetadata`, `inspectDesign`, `viewDesign`, `exportDesign`,\n`placeDesignImage`, `putDesignImage`, `listDesignFonts`, `installDesignFonts {families}`, `uploadDesignFont {source}`,\n`listDesignIcons`, `listDesignTemplates`, `readDesignTemplate`, `insertDesignTemplate`, `editDesign`, comments\n(`listDesignComments`, `addDesignComment`, `setDesignCommentStatus`), `getStyleGuide`, page building\n(`previewDesignPage`, `buildDesignPage`, `reviewDesignPageUpdate`, `applyDesignPageUpdate`), `readCanvasGuide {topic}`.\n",
 "gotchas": "# gotchas: mistakes that cost a re-run\n\nMost of these are the same in Figma; the Canvas-specific ones say so.\n\n## resize() resets sizing to FIXED\n```js\n// WRONG: the frame stays 300×10 forever\nf.layoutMode = 'VERTICAL'; f.primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'; f.resize(300, 10)\n// RIGHT: resize first, then ask it to hug\nf.layoutMode = 'VERTICAL'; f.resize(300, 10); f.primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'\n// or: figma.createAutoLayout('VERTICAL') and give it a width with layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FIXED' + resize before HUG on the other axis\n```\n\n## FILL and HUG need the right context\n`layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FILL'` only works on a child of an auto-layout frame: `parent.appendChild(child)` first.\n`HUG` works on auto-layout frames and text. `primaryAxisSizingMode` takes `FIXED | AUTO`, never `HUG` or `FILL`.\n\n## Wrapping text needs HEIGHT and a width\n```js\nt.textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT'; t.resize(880, t.height)   // wraps at 880\n// in an auto-layout column: parent.appendChild(t); t.layoutSizingHorizontal = 'FILL'; t.textAutoResize = 'HEIGHT'\n```\n`WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT` (the default) never wraps; `\\n` is the only line break.\n\n## Fonts\n- `await figma.loadFontAsync(...)` before `characters`, `fontName`, `fontSize`, range calls or styles that use the font.\n- Use Figma's style names: `SemiBold`, not `Semibold` or `Semi Bold`; `Bold Italic`, not `BoldItalic`.\n- SF Pro, Helvetica Neue and other system fonts are not Google fonts: use Inter (or upload the brand file once with\n  `uploadDesignFont {source}`).\n- Canvas installs Google fonts with every static weight and the optical-size axis, so DM Sans, Inter and Roboto Flex match\n  Figma's letter fit at every size.\n\n## Rotation turns around the top-left corner\nAs in Figma, `rotation` (and `relativeTransform`) pivots on the node's own top-left corner, so `x`/`y` stay the corner's\nposition. To rotate around the centre, compute the corner:\n```js\nconst cx = x + w / 2, cy = y + h / 2, a = angle * Math.PI / 180\nnode.rotation = angle\nnode.x = cx - (w / 2) * Math.cos(a) - (h / 2) * Math.sin(a)\nnode.y = cy + (w / 2) * Math.sin(a) - (h / 2) * Math.cos(a)\n```\nAuto-sized text that grows after it was rotated keeps its top-left corner where it was, as in Figma.\n\n## Colours\n0–1, not 0–255. Put alpha on the paint's `opacity` (Canvas also folds a `color.a` on SOLID paints into the opacity, Figma does not).\nGradient stops do take `{ r, g, b, a }`.\n\n## Gradient direction\n`gradientTransform` maps the layer's unit square into gradient space, where the gradient runs from x = 0 to x = 1.\nIdentity `[[1,0,0],[0,1,0]]` = left → right. Top → bottom: `[[0,1,0],[-1,0,1]]`. Bottom → top: `[[0,-1,1],[1,0,0]]`.\nFor a CSS angle θ (0 = up, clockwise), with r = θ·π/180:\n`[[Math.sin(r), -Math.cos(r), 0.5 - Math.sin(r)/2 + Math.cos(r)/2], [Math.cos(r), Math.sin(r), 0.5 - Math.cos(r)/2 - Math.sin(r)/2]]`.\n\n## Arrays are replaced, not mutated\n`node.fills[0].color = …` does nothing. `node.fills = [{ ...node.fills[0], color: … }]`.\n`setBoundVariableForPaint` returns a new paint: reassign it.\n\n## Masks clip the siblings above them\n`isMask = true` on a layer turns it into a mask for every later sibling in the same parent, up to the next mask. The usual\nidiom is `figma.group([maskShape, picture], parent)` with the mask first. The mask itself is not drawn. For a plain rounded\ncrop a frame with `clipsContent = true` and `cornerRadius` is simpler.\n\n## Instance layers\nChange only `characters`, `visible`, text ranges or nested swaps on an instance's layers; they become overrides. For\nanything else (resize a child, recolour a rectangle) `detachInstance()` first, or change the main component.\n\n## Emoji\nColour emoji draw from Noto Color Emoji at Figma's emoji size (one em wide, centred on the line). Figma's own renderer shows\nApple-style artwork, so emoji look like the Noto set, not like iOS. An emoji-only text with AUTO line height is as tall as\nits font size, as in Figma. Emoji whose default is text (❤ ☺ ✔) draw as plain glyphs in the text colour unless followed by\nU+FE0F, as in Figma.\n\n## Things Canvas does not have (they throw, with the alternative)\nVariants and component properties, team libraries, paint/effect/grid styles, sections, slices, text on a path,\n`vectorNetwork`, `arcData`, `flatten`, `outlineStroke`, angular/diamond gradients, progressive blur, noise/texture/glass effects,\n`exportAsync` (use `viewDesign`/`exportDesign`), `createImage(bytes)` (use `createImageAsync`), more than one page.\n",
 "text": "# text: Canvas's text model (it is Figma's)\n\nText is shaped and measured with Skia's paragraph engine (HarfBuzz) and the project's real font files, and drawn by the same\nengine in `viewDesign` and `exportDesign`. Sizes you read back in a script (`t.width`, `t.height`) are the measured ones.\n\n## Line height\n- `{ unit: 'AUTO' }` (the default for new text) is the font's own line height: (ascender + descender + line gap) / em, from\n  the font's horizontal header, as Figma uses. Inter ≈ 121%, Poppins 150%, DM Sans ≈ 130%, Caveat ≈ 126%.\n- `{ unit: 'PERCENT', value: 110 }` and `{ unit: 'PIXELS', value: 72 }` are exact; extra space is shared above and below the\n  line (half-leading), so the first baseline moves as in Figma.\n- An emoji-only text with AUTO takes the emoji font's line box (one em).\n- Changing `fontSize` keeps a PIXELS line height in pixels, as Figma does.\n\n## Letter spacing\n`{ unit: 'PERCENT', value: -2 }` is a percentage of the font size; `{ unit: 'PIXELS', value: 1.5 }` is absolute.\n\n## Auto-resize\n- `WIDTH_AND_HEIGHT`: one line per `\\n`, the box hugs the text.\n- `HEIGHT`: fixed width, wraps on word boundaries, the box grows down. Words longer than the width break.\n- `NONE`: fixed box; text that does not fit overflows (it is not clipped unless a parent clips).\n- `TRUNCATE` / `textTruncation = 'ENDING'` with `maxLines`: ends with an ellipsis.\nA line that only just fits can wrap one word differently from Figma (sub-pixel advance differences); leave a few pixels of\nslack in fixed-width headlines, and check with `viewDesign`.\n\n## Mixed styles in one text\n`setRangeFontName`, `setRangeFontSize`, `setRangeFills`, `setRangeTextDecoration`, `setRangeLetterSpacing`, `setRangeLineHeight`\nover `[start, end)`. A mixed line takes the tallest line height of its runs. `getStyledTextSegments(['fontName', 'fills', …])`\nreads them back. Load every font a range uses before setting it. Changing `characters` drops the ranges (set them after).\n\n## Alignment\n`textAlignHorizontal LEFT | CENTER | RIGHT | JUSTIFIED`, `textAlignVertical TOP | CENTER | BOTTOM` (inside a fixed box).\n\n## Text on photos\nContrast comes from the layers under the text, never from the text itself: a gradient wash rectangle (`GRADIENT_LINEAR`\nfrom 0.85 alpha to 0), a dark rounded panel at 0.6–0.8 opacity, or a `DROP_SHADOW` on the text with radius 8–16 and\nalpha 0.35–0.5. `LAYER_BLUR` on a copy of the photo behind a panel, or `BACKGROUND_BLUR` on the panel itself, gives frosted glass.\n\n## Fonts\n- Any Google family by name with `loadFontAsync`; variable families get every weight and their optical-size axis (opsz =\n  font size, as Figma's auto optical sizing).\n- Brand files: `uploadDesignFont {source: '/path/Font-Bold.otf'}` once per project, then `loadFontAsync` by family name.\n- No limit on fonts per project.\n- Symbols (★ ✓ ✕ → ⌕ ✎) that a font lacks fall back to Noto Sans Symbols 2; colour emoji to Noto Color Emoji.\n- A character no installed font has is reported in `unmeasuredText` (`missing-glyph`) and in `viewDesign` notes: fix it.\n",
 "paints-effects-masks": "# paints-effects-masks: fills, gradients, pictures, shadows, blurs, blend modes, masks and corners\n\n## Paints (fills and strokes)\n```js\n{ type: 'SOLID', color: { r, g, b }, opacity: 1 }\n{ type: 'GRADIENT_LINEAR', gradientTransform: [[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0]], gradientStops: [{ position: 0, color: { r, g, b, a } }, …] }\n{ type: 'GRADIENT_RADIAL', gradientTransform: [[1, 0, 0], [0, 1, 0]], gradientStops: [...] }   // centre 0.5,0.5, radius 0.5 of the box\n{ type: 'IMAGE', imageHash: img.hash, scaleMode: 'FILL' | 'FIT' | 'CROP' | 'TILE' | 'STRETCH', filters: { exposure: 0.1, contrast: 0.2, saturation: -1, temperature: 0.3, tint: 0, highlights: -0.2, shadows: 0.2 } }\n```\n- Several fills stack bottom to top; each has its own `opacity`, `visible` and `blendMode`.\n- CROP: `imageTransform: [[sx, 0, tx], [0, sy, ty]]` is the visible window of the picture (as in Figma). `scalingFactor` sets TILE size.\n- Image filters (−1..1) are baked into the export: saturation −1 is black and white, temperature > 0 warmer.\n- Strokes: `strokeWeight`, `strokeAlign INSIDE | CENTER | OUTSIDE`, per-side weights on frames and rectangles, `dashPattern [10, 6]`,\n  `strokeCap`, `strokeJoin`. A stroke-only ellipse is a ring.\n\n## Effects\n```js\nnode.effects = [\n  { type: 'DROP_SHADOW', color: { r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 0.25 }, offset: { x: 0, y: 8 }, radius: 24, spread: 0, visible: true, blendMode: 'NORMAL' },\n  { type: 'INNER_SHADOW', color: { r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 0.14 }, offset: { x: 0, y: -3 }, radius: 0, spread: 0, visible: true, blendMode: 'NORMAL' },\n  { type: 'LAYER_BLUR', blurType: 'NORMAL', radius: 40, visible: true },\n  { type: 'BACKGROUND_BLUR', blurType: 'NORMAL', radius: 30, visible: true },\n]\n```\n- Blur radius means what it means in Figma (Gaussian sigma = radius / 2).\n- `BACKGROUND_BLUR` blurs everything drawn behind the layer, inside the layer's shape, under its own fill: give the layer a\n  semi-transparent fill (white at 0.6–0.85 for iOS frosted panels).\n- A blurred picture that bleeds past the frame keeps solid edges, as in Figma.\n- Shadows on text follow the glyphs, as in Figma.\n\n## Blend modes\n`node.blendMode` and per-paint `blendMode`: NORMAL, MULTIPLY, SCREEN, OVERLAY, DARKEN, LIGHTEN, COLOR_DODGE, COLOR_BURN,\nHARD_LIGHT, SOFT_LIGHT, DIFFERENCE, EXCLUSION, HUE, SATURATION, COLOR, LUMINOSITY (and PASS_THROUGH on groups and frames).\nTypical ad uses: a tone rectangle in MULTIPLY to darken a photo, SOFT_LIGHT for a warm glow, SCREEN for light leaks.\n\n## Masks and clipping\n- `frame.clipsContent = true` clips children to the frame's shape, including `cornerRadius` and `cornerSmoothing`.\n- `isMask = true`: the layer masks every later sibling in its parent (until the next mask) and is not drawn itself.\n  `maskType = 'ALPHA'` (default, the mask's opacity), `'VECTOR'` (its outline), `'LUMINANCE'` (its brightness).\n```js\n// circular zoom of a photo with a thick ring: the mask clips the picture after it in the same group\nconst disc = figma.createEllipse(); disc.resize(420, 420); disc.isMask = true\nconst pic = figma.createRectangle(); pic.resize(420, 420)\npic.fills = [{ type: 'IMAGE', imageHash: img.hash, scaleMode: 'CROP', imageTransform: [[0.3, 0, 0.55], [0, 0.3, 0.2]] }]\nad.appendChild(disc); ad.appendChild(pic)\nconst zoom = figma.group([disc, pic], ad); zoom.name = 'Zoom'; zoom.x = 600; zoom.y = 300\nconst ring = figma.createEllipse(); ad.appendChild(ring); ring.resize(420, 420); ring.x = 600; ring.y = 300\nring.fills = []; ring.strokes = [figma.util.solidPaint('#ffd400')]; ring.strokeWeight = 14; ring.strokeAlign = 'INSIDE'\n```\nA frame with `clipsContent = true` and `cornerRadius` = half its size does the same for a plain circle.\n\n## Corners\n`cornerRadius`, per-corner radii, and `cornerSmoothing` 0–1 (0.6 = iOS squircle) on frames, rectangles and components; it\napplies to fills, strokes, clipping and shadows.\n",
 "vectors-icons": "# vectors-icons: paths, SVG, booleans, arrows and icons\n\n## Icons: import SVG, never rebuild from rotated rectangles\n```js\nconst icon = figma.createNodeFromSvg(canvas.icon('search', { color: '#5f6368', size: 32, strokeWidth: 2 }))\nbar.appendChild(icon)          // a frame holding one vector per SVG shape\nconst g = figma.createNodeFromSvg(canvas.icon('google-g', { size: 40 }))   // the four-colour G\n```\n`canvas.icons('chart')` (or the `listDesignIcons {query}` operation) lists what exists: 67 line icons and 17 brand marks.\nAny SVG you write yourself works too: paths, rect/circle/ellipse/line/polyline/polygon, `<g transform>`, viewBox, `<use>`,\nstroke caps/joins/dashes, `fill-rule`, opacity, linear and radial gradient fills. Text, images, filters, clip paths and masks\ninside the SVG are left out and named in `warnings`: add them as Canvas layers.\n\n## Vectors\n```js\nconst v = figma.createVector()\nv.vectorPaths = [{ windingRule: 'NONZERO', data: 'M0 40 C 60 0, 120 80, 180 30' }]   // any SVG path syntax (relative, arcs, H/V)\nv.strokes = [figma.util.solidPaint('#e53935')]; v.strokeWeight = 6; v.strokeCap = 'ROUND'; v.strokeJoin = 'ROUND'; v.fills = []\n```\n`vectorNetwork` throws: use `vectorPaths` or `createNodeFromSvg`.\n\n## Hand-drawn arrows (for \"That's you →\" callouts)\n```js\nconst arrow = figma.createNodeFromSvg(`<svg width=\"220\" height=\"160\" viewBox=\"0 0 220 160\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e53935\" stroke-width=\"7\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">\n  <path d=\"M12 20 C 80 10, 170 40, 190 128\"/><path d=\"M160 112 L 190 132 L 204 98\"/></svg>`)\nad.appendChild(arrow); arrow.x = 640; arrow.y = 980; arrow.rotation = -6\n```\n\n## Shapes\n`createRectangle`, `createEllipse` (pie/donut via SVG path; `arcData` throws), `createStar` (`pointCount`, `innerRadius`),\n`createPolygon` (`pointCount`), `createLine` (a 1 px line along x: `resize(length, 0)`, `strokeWeight`, `strokes`, `rotation`).\n\n## Booleans\n`figma.union([a, b], parent)`, `subtract`, `intersect`, `exclude` make a real boolean shape (first child's fill). Useful for\nspeech bubbles (rounded rect ∪ triangle), cut-out badges (circle − circle), ticket shapes.\n`figma.flatten` throws: keep the boolean, or union the parts.\n\n## Sparklines and charts\nBuild the path from data:\n```js\nconst pts = [12, 18, 15, 26, 31, 29, 44]\nconst d = pts.map((y, i) => `${i ? 'L' : 'M'}${i * 40} ${100 - y * 2}`).join(' ')\nconst line = figma.createVector(); line.vectorPaths = [{ windingRule: 'NONZERO', data: d }]\nline.fills = []; line.strokes = [figma.util.solidPaint('#34a853')]; line.strokeWeight = 4; line.strokeJoin = 'ROUND'\n```\n",
 "components-variables-styles": "# components-variables-styles: components, instances, variables, modes and text styles\n\n## Components and instances\n```js\nconst chip = figma.createComponent()\nchip.name = 'Chip'; chip.layoutMode = 'HORIZONTAL'; chip.primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'; chip.counterAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'\nchip.paddingLeft = 16; chip.paddingRight = 16; chip.paddingTop = 8; chip.paddingBottom = 8; chip.cornerRadius = 10\nconst label = figma.createText(); label.name = 'Label'; chip.appendChild(label); label.characters = 'label'\nfor (const text of ['❌ page 4 on Google', '❌ unseen by ChatGPT']) {\n  const inst = chip.createInstance(); list.appendChild(inst)\n  inst.findOne(n => n.type === 'TEXT' && n.name === 'Label').characters = text   // an override; the instance stays linked\n}\nfigma.currentPage.appendChild(chip); chip.x = ad.x; chip.y = ad.y + ad.height + 80   // keep masters off the artboard\n```\n- Overrides on instance layers: `characters`, `visible`, text range styles, nested `swapComponent`. Other changes throw and\n  say to `detachInstance()` (or change the main component, which updates every instance).\n- `instance.mainComponent`, `await instance.getMainComponentAsync()`, `instance.swapComponent(other)`, `instance.detachInstance()`.\n- `figma.createComponentFromNode(frame)` turns an existing frame or group into a component.\n- Not yet: variants (`combineAsVariants`), component properties (`setProperties`, `addComponentProperty`). Make one component\n  per variant and swap; set instance layers directly.\n\n## Variables\nOne collection per design (\"Brand\") with a base mode; add modes for brands or themes.\n```js\nconst c = (await figma.variables.getLocalVariableCollectionsAsync())[0]\nconst ink = figma.variables.createVariable('color/ink', c, 'COLOR')\nink.setValueForMode(c.modes[0].modeId, { r: 0.08, g: 0.09, b: 0.23 })\nconst radius = figma.variables.createVariable('radius/card', c, 'FLOAT'); radius.setValueForMode(c.modes[0].modeId, 22)\ncard.fills = [figma.variables.setBoundVariableForPaint(figma.util.solidPaint('#000000'), 'color', ink)]\ncard.setBoundVariable('cornerRadius', radius)\nconst dark = c.addMode('Dark'); ink.setValueForMode(dark, { r: 1, g: 1, b: 1 }); ad.setExplicitVariableModeForCollection(c, dark)\n```\n- Types: `COLOR` and `FLOAT`. `STRING` and `BOOLEAN` throw (use text styles for fonts). Aliases between variables throw.\n- Bindable: paint colour, `cornerRadius` and per-corner radii, `itemSpacing`, `counterAxisSpacing`, paddings, `strokeWeight`,\n  `fontSize`, `lineHeight`, `letterSpacing`, `paragraphSpacing`, `width`/`height` and min/max sizes.\n- `variable.scopes` and code syntax are accepted for compatibility but do not change anything in Canvas.\n\n## Text styles\n```js\nconst h = figma.createTextStyle(); h.name = 'display/xl'\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({ family: 'Poppins', style: 'Bold' })\nh.fontName = { family: 'Poppins', style: 'Bold' }; h.fontSize = 72; h.lineHeight = { unit: 'PERCENT', value: 105 }\nheadline.textStyleId = h.id\n```\nChanging a style updates every text that uses it. Paint, effect and grid styles do not exist in Canvas: use COLOR variables\nfor shared colours and a shared `effects` array in your script for shadows.\n\n## Templates as a design system\n`listDesignTemplates {query, category}` → `insertDesignTemplate {designId, templateId, expectedRevision}` adds a finished ad\nframe that shares the design's Brand collection and text styles. Re-brand it in one script: add a mode, set the colour\nvariables, point the `display/`, `body/`, `strong/` and `quote/` text styles at the brand fonts, fill the named text layers.\n",
 "validation-and-recovery": "# validation-and-recovery: checking your work\n\n## What every script result tells you\n```json\n{ \"revision\": 7, \"result\": { \"frame\": \"…\" }, \"created\": 23,\n  \"logs\": [\"…console.log output…\"],\n  \"warnings\": [\"createNodeFromSvg: Text inside the SVG was left out; add it as a TEXT layer.\"],\n  \"unmeasuredText\": [{ \"id\": \"…\", \"code\": \"missing-glyph\", \"family\": \"Montserrat\" }] }\n```\n- `warnings`: something was approximated or left out; each says what to do instead. Expect none on a finished ad.\n- `unmeasuredText`: text Canvas could not measure: `missing-family` / `missing-style` (load the font), `missing-glyph`\n  (a character no font has; change it or load a font that has it), `budget` (an absurdly long text).\n\n## Structure: getDesignMetadata\n`getDesignMetadata {designId, nodeId?, depth?}` returns an XML outline like Figma's `get_metadata`:\n```xml\n<frame id=\"…\" name=\"Ad\" x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1080\" height=\"1920\" fills=\"image:fill\" clipsContent=\"true\">\n  <text id=\"…\" name=\"Headline\" x=\"80\" y=\"260\" width=\"920\" height=\"186\" font=\"DM Sans 700 88\" text=\"Get found on Google\" />\n  <instance id=\"…\" name=\"Chip\" x=\"52\" y=\"709\" width=\"377\" height=\"69\" mainComponent=\"…\" />\n```\nCheck sizes, wraps (height ÷ line height = lines), positions and that nothing sits outside the frame, without a screenshot.\n`inspectDesign` gives a compact per-frame summary; `readDesign` the full JSON (large).\n\n## Pixels: viewDesign\n`viewDesign {designId, artboardId, scale}` renders with the export's renderer and fonts: at `scale: 1` it equals\n`exportDesign`. Use `scale: 0.5` for a 1080×1920 check, `top`/`height` to look at one band at full size. Its notes list\nsubstituted fonts, missing pictures and missing glyphs.\n\n## Look for\n- Words cut off, overlapping or wrapping one word onto a new line; text too close to the edges (keep 9:16 copy out of the\n  top 270 px and bottom 670 px for Reels/Stories UI).\n- Pictures missing or cropped wrong (`scaleMode`, `imageTransform`).\n- Contrast of text on photos.\n- Shapes you meant to rotate around their centre that moved (rotation pivots on the top-left corner).\n\n## Recovering\n- A script that throws changes nothing: fix and re-run with the same `expectedRevision`.\n- `expectedRevision` mismatch: `getDesignMetadata` (it is cheap), then continue from the current state.\n- Undo a bad change: run a script that removes or resets the nodes (`figma.getNodeById(id).remove()`), or rebuild the frame:\n  remove it by name at the start of the script so re-runs are idempotent:\n  `for (const n of figma.currentPage.children.filter(n => n.name === 'Ad 9:16')) n.remove()`.\n\n## Error messages and what they mean\n| Message | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `Font \"Poppins SemiBold\" has no such style. Installed styles: …` | Use one of the listed styles, or check the family on Google Fonts. |\n| `Cannot write to node with unloaded font \"X Y\"` | `await figma.loadFontAsync({ family: 'X', style: 'Y' })` first. |\n| `object is not extensible: TEXT \"Title\" has no property \"fontWeight\"` | Not a Figma property (or read-only): use `fontName`. |\n| `x is not supported in Canvas yet. …` | A Figma feature Canvas lacks; follow the alternative in the message. |\n| `Cannot set properties of null (setting 'characters')` | `findOne` found nothing: check the name and type you searched for. |\n| `The script made an invalid design: layer \"Bad\" (rectangle, width): …` | A value out of range (negative, NaN, huge); the layer and property are named. |\n| `Unknown imageHash` | Use `(await figma.createImageAsync(source)).hash`. |\n| `Range a..b is outside the text (length n)` | Compute ranges from the final `characters`. |\n",
 "figma-tools": "# figma-tools: Figma's MCP tools and their Canvas equivalents\n\nFigma's MCP server has 46 tools. These are the ones that matter for designing ads, and what to use in Canvas instead.\n\n| Figma tool | What it does | Canvas |\n|---|---|---|\n| `use_figma` | Run Plugin API JavaScript | `runCanvasScript {designId, expectedRevision, code}` (same API) |\n| `create_new_file` | New design file | `createDesign {title}` |\n| `create_session` | File session | Not needed: `workspaceId`/`projectId` is supplied by the host |\n| `get_screenshot` | Picture of a node | `viewDesign {designId, artboardId, scale, top?, height?}` (= the export) |\n| `get_metadata` | XML layer outline | `getDesignMetadata {designId, nodeId?, depth?}` |\n| `get_design_context` | Code + screenshot for design-to-code | `inspectDesign`, `getDesignMetadata`, `readDesign`; pages: `previewDesignPage` / `buildDesignPage` |\n| `get_variable_defs` | Variables and styles used | `getDesignSystem {designId}` |\n| `search_design_system`, `get_libraries` | Find components/styles in libraries | `getDesignSystem`, `listDesignTemplates {query, category}`, `readDesignTemplate`, `getStyleGuide` |\n| `upload_assets` | Put pictures into the file | `figma.createImageAsync(path \\| URL)` in scripts, `putDesignImage {source}`, `placeDesignImage {nodeId, source, scaleMode}` |\n| `download_assets` | Export node pictures | `exportDesign {designId, artboardId, scale}` (writes the PNG, returns its path) |\n| `generate_vector_illustration` | AI vector art | `canvas.icon(name)` (67 line icons, 17 brand marks) + `figma.createNodeFromSvg(svg)` for SVG you write; no AI generation |\n| `generate_image` | AI picture | Not in Canvas (paid; Studio's `generate_image` asks the user to approve). Reuse project pictures. |\n| `get_comments` | Read comments | `listDesignComments`, `addDesignComment`, `setDesignCommentStatus` |\n| `generate_figma_design` | Capture a web page as a design | Not in Canvas; rebuild with a script, or use page building for Studio pages |\n| `whoami` | Account | Not needed |\n| Fonts (inside `use_figma`) | `loadFontAsync`, `listAvailableFontsAsync` | Same, plus `installDesignFonts {families}`, `uploadDesignFont {source}`, `listDesignFonts` |\n\nNot relevant to ads (no Canvas equivalent planned): Code Connect (`get_code_connect_map`, `add_code_connect_map`,\n`get_code_connect_suggestions`, `send_code_connect_mappings`, `get_context_for_code_connect`), FigJam and diagrams\n(`get_figjam`, `generate_diagram`), motion and video (`get_motion_context`, `export_video`), shaders and generative plugins\n(`list_file_shaders`, `list_shaders`, `get_shader`, `create_shader`, `update_shader`, `list_generative_plugins`,\n`get_generative_plugin`, `create_generative_plugin`, `update_generative_plugin`), branching (`create_branch`),\n`send_code_to_figma`, and the Weave model runner (`weave_*`, 10 tools).\n"
};
